// tests/fixtures/ambiguous_decls/cycle_self.nv
// Phase 0 adversarial fixture: SELF-REFERENCE classification cycle (A → A).
//
// To classify `Loop`, the resolver inspects its body and finds a call
// expression `Loop()`. To determine if `Loop` is a component-builder (calls
// resolve to functions/macros) or a struct (no calls), it needs to know what
// `Loop` resolves to — but that's the very declaration being classified.
//
// This MUST produce a "declaration classification cycle" diagnostic (E0010),
// NOT infinite recursion or a silent guess.
//
// --- Why the previous version was wrong ---
// The previous fixture was:
//     Node:
//         next: Node
// That is a field declaration (`identifier: type_expr`), not a call. Field
// type references do NOT require classifying the referenced declaration — they
// only look up the name as a type. There is no classification dependency there;
// it becomes a type-layout error (recursive struct without indirection) at a
// later stage, not a classification cycle. A genuine cycle requires a CALL
// expression whose callee's classification is unknown.
//
// (EXECUTION_GUIDE.md Phase 0 precision points; COMPILER_ARCHITECTURE.md §4)
//
// Expected: error E0010 "declaration classification cycle" on Loop
// Expected golden: tests/golden/ambiguous_decls/cycle_self.json

Loop:
    Loop()
